Article 5 (Special cases concerning age requirements for examination eligibility)
Notwithstanding the amended provisions of Article 24(3), a person who is at least 18 years of age in the relevant year may apply for a recruitment examination for professional civilian military employees or civilian military employees in general service for a fixed term position of Grade VIII or lower conducted through 2019.
Article 6 (Transitional measures concerning changes in classification of civilian military employees due to abolition of technical and contract-based civilian military employees)
(1) A civilian military employee who, as of December 21, 2017 (hereinafter referred to as the "enforcement date of the Act"), was serving in the ranks, grades, occupational groups, and series listed in the left column of the following table under former Appendix 2 shall be deemed appointed as a civilian military employee in general service of the ranks, grades, occupational groups, and series listed in the right column of the same table pursuant to the amended provisions of Appendix 1.												<tbl_group>																				<tbl_group></tbl_group>																				<tbl_group></tbl_group></tbl_group>												<tbl_group></tbl_group>
(2) Where other statutes, at the time of the date of enforcement of the Act, cite the grades of civilian military employees listed in the left column of the table under paragraph (1), such grades shall be deemed to refer to the grades of civilian military employees in general service listed in the right column of the same table.
(3) Contract-based civilian military employees in service as of the date of enforcement of the Act shall be deemed appointed as civilian military employees in general service for a fixed term position according to the following classifications:
1. Former general contract-based civilian military employees under Article 133(2): fixed-term civilian military employees in general service of the rank, position, or duty level corresponding to the position held at the time of enforcement of the Act;
2. Former professional contract-based civilian military employees under Article 133(3): professional fixed-term civilian military employees in general service.
(4) For a person deemed appointed as a civilian military employee in general service for a fixed term position under paragraph (3), when calculating the total period of service pursuant to Article 22-5 of the Decree on the Appointment of Public Officials as applied mutatis mutandis under the amended provisions of Article 137, the date on which the person was initially employed as a contract-based civilian military employee shall be deemed the date of initial appointment as a civilian military employee in general service for a fixed term position.
Article 7 (Transitional measures concerning classification of experience)
Where a person who was a technical civilian military employee at the time of enforcement of the Act is appointed as a civilian military employee in general service, the classification of prior experience as a technical civilian military employee shall be deemed classified under the amended provisions of Article 77, according to the following distinctions:
1. Experience as a technical civilian military employee in a grade equal to or higher than the current grade, where the person has been converted to a civilian military employee in general service of the administrative services occupational group: Grade A experience;
2. Experience in a grade equal to or higher than the former grade prior to conversion or appointment from a technical civilian military employee to a civilian military employee in general service: Grade B experience;
3. Experience as a technical civilian military employee of the immediately lower grade where the person has been converted to a civilian military employee in general service of the administrative services occupational group: Grade C experience.
Article 8 (Transitional measures concerning appointment by promotion)
(1) The performance evaluation scores, performance goal evaluation scores, career evaluation scores, additional point scores, and disciplinary records of former technical, exceptional, or contract-based civilian military employees before the enforcement of the Act shall remain valid and may be reflected in appointment by promotion, performance bonus payment, etc. (hereinafter referred to as "appointment by promotion, etc.") after they are appointed as civilian military employees in general service.
(2) Notwithstanding paragraph (1), the performance evaluation scores of technical and exceptional civilian military employees in service at the time of the enforcement of the Act shall not be reflected in appointment by promotion, etc., according to the following classifications:
1. Where a technical civilian military employee in service at the time of enforcement of the Act is appointed through conversion pursuant to Article 3 of the Special Rules on Transfer Appointment Following Changes in Classification of Civilian Military Employees: Performance evalu ation scores received while serving as a technical civilian military employee and as a civilian military employee in general service of the administrative services occupational group under Appendix 1, item 10 shall not be reflected after such transfer appointment;
2. Where an exceptional civilian military employee in service at the time of enforcement of the Act is appointed as a dedicated-position civilian military employee in general service pursuant to Article 8(1) of the Special Rules on Transfer Appointment Following Changes in Classification of Civilian Military Employees, and the designation of the dedicated position is later canceled pursuant to paragraph (3) of the same Article: Performance evaluation scores received before the cancellation of the dedicated position shall not be reflected after the cancellation.
(3) Where a person who was a technical or contract-based civilian military employee before the enforcement of the Act retires and is newly appointed as a civilian military employee in general service after the enforcement, the recognition of service experience shall be governed by former Articles 10, 39, and 43-2. In such cases, service in a grade listed in the left column of the table under Article 6(1) of the Addenda shall be deemed equivalent to service in the grade listed in the right column of the same table.
(4) Where a civilian military employee in general service was appointed as a technical civilian military employee, or a technical civilian military employee was appointed as a civilian military employee in general service before the enforcement of the Act, the period of service already counted under former Article 39(3) and Article 43-2(2) shall continue to be valid and counted after the enforcement.
(5) Promotion candidate lists and deliberations or resolutions of promotion screening committees for promotion of former technical civilian military employees in progress at the time of enforcement of the Act shall remain valid.
Article 9 Omitted.

