ADDENDA <Presidential Decree No. 32155, Nov. 30, 2021>
Article 1 (Enforcement date)
This Decree shall enter into force on the date of its promulgation; provided, the amended provisions of Articles 39(9) and 43-2(3) shall enter into force 1 year after the date of promulgation.
Article 2 (Applicability to calculation of minimum service period required for promotion and service period for seniority-based promotion)
The amended provisions of Articles 39(9) and 43-2(3) shall also apply to the calculation of the minimum service period required for promotion and the service period for seniority-based promotion for civilian military employees in general service who are in service as of the enforcement date under the proviso of Article 1 of Addenda.
Article 3 (Applicability to calculation of annual leave period following changes to the leave system)
When calculating the maximum period of leave pursuant to the amended provisions of Article 54(2) and (3), the period of leave used under the former Article 54(2) before the enforcement of this Decree shall be included.
Article 4 (Transitional measures concerning determination of additional successful candidates for examinations)
Notwithstanding the amended provisions of Article 18(5), the determination of additional successful candidates for open competitive examinations or career-based competitive examinations for appointment (excluding civilian military employees of Grade I in general service), for which final successful candidates were announced before the enforcement of this Decree, shall be governed by the previous provisions.

